cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use verdict-contract in research or software, please cite it as below."
title: "verdict-contract: a parseable verdict contract for LLM review gates"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dziatkovskii
    given-names: Anton
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7408-3054"
    affiliation: "Palo Alto AI Research Lab"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Palo-Alto-AI-Research-Lab/verdict-contract"
url: "https://github.com/Palo-Alto-AI-Research-Lab/verdict-contract"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - LLM evaluation
  - code review automation
  - AI agents
  - fail-safe design
  - prompt injection
abstract: >-
  A ~200-line stdlib-only Python module that makes an LLM reviewer's verdict
  machine-checkable: a whole-line sentinel marker, a closed enum with an explicit
  AMBIGUOUS state, a weak layer that can block but never approve, and an exit-code
  gate. Prompt rule and parser live in one file so the contract cannot drift. The
  42 test cases are counterexamples produced by vendor models over seven adversarial
  rounds against the authors' own review gate.
